                <pb facs="1098" n="1076" sameAs="frus:frus1950v05/pg1076"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>The President of the General Assembly put the draft resolution on Jerusalem
                    contained in the report of the <hi rendition="#italic">Ad Hoc</hi> Political
                    Committee to a vote on December 15. There was no discussion of the measure. The
                    result was thirty votes in favor, eighteen opposed, and nine abstentions. The
                    United States and the United Kingdom were recorded in opposition; the Soviet
                    Union abstained. Inasmuch as the measure failed to obtain the required
                    two-thirds majority, the draft resolution failed of adoption (GA (V), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Plenary</hi>, page 684).</p>
            </div>
        </body>
